    "body": "## Motivation\n\nSame loss pattern as #41909 / #41914 / #41962 / #41963 / #42007:\n`Llama32Detector` and `DotsToolDetector` hold text back in `self._buffer`\nwhile waiting for the closing marker, and `BaseFormatDetector.finish()`\nreturns an empty result by default. When the stream ends with an incomplete\ntool call still buffered, the held-back text is silently dropped:\n\n- `Llama32Detector`: the whole python block (including preceding normal\n  text) is kept in `_buffer` until the call can be resolved; at end of\n  stream it is lost.\n- `DotsToolDetector`: a partial `<dots_function_call>` invoke block is\n  lost at end of stream.\n\n## Changes\n\nAdd a `finish()` override to each detector that flushes `_buffer` as normal\ntext:\n\n- `Llama32Detector`: flush the buffered python block.\n- `DotsToolDetector`: flush the buffered partial invoke block; a pure\n  trailing closing tag (`</dots_function_call>`) is syntax residue and is\n  not re-emitted.\n\nNormal streams are unaffected: `finish()` stays a no-op when `_buffer` is\nempty.\n\n## Tests\n\nOffline unit tests (no server, no model loading) for each detector cover:\n- partial tool call at stream end: `finish()` releases the buffered text;\n- clean stream: `finish()` returns an empty result;\n- complete-call behavior: the buffered block is flushed rather than dropped.\n\nAll pass locally (`pytest test/registered/unit/function_call/test_{llama32,dots}_detector_finish.py`), ruff clean (ignoring pre-existing E722 warnings in `llama32_detector.py`).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #37403229170](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37403229170)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #37403228801](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37403228801)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #37403229132](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37403229132)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
